==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|la|en}} {{term|cochlea||snail|lang=la}}, from {{etyl|grc|en}} {{term|κοχλίας||spiral, snail shell|tr=kokhlias|lang=grc}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈkɒk.lɪə/}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|s|cochleae}}

# {{context|anatomy|lang=en}} The complex, spirally coiled, tapered [[cavity]] of the [[inner ear]] in which sound vibrations are converted into nerve impulses.

====Derived terms====
* [[cochlear]]

